  "finalText": "The cancel job capability is **already fully implemented** across all three layers. All 32 related tests pass. Here's a summary of what exists:\n\n### Store layer\n- `JobStore.save()` persists `JobRecord` (including `cancelRequested` flag) to `jobs/<id>.json` — `apps/server/src/job-store.ts:22`\n- `BenchmarkStore.updateSuiteStatus()` durably marks suite status to `\"cancelled\"` — used by both the job body `finally` block and the API route\n\n### Job/process layer (`apps/server/src/jobs.ts`)\n- `JobManager.cancel(id)` (line 175): validates the job exists and is `queued`|`running`, returns `false` for already-finished jobs\n- For **queued** jobs: immediately removes from queue, marks `status: \"cancelled\"`, cancels pending stages\n- For **running** jobs: sets `cancelRequested = true`; the job body observes it via `ctx.throwIfCancelled()` at stage transitions and between tasks (line 265-268)\n- `runBenchmarkJob` in `apps/server/src/benchmark.ts:230-233`: the `finally` block marks the suite cancelled in the store and calls `markSuiteInterrupted()` when `ctx.job.cancelRequested` is true\n\n### API layer (`apps/server/src/routes.ts`)\n- `POST /jobs/:id/cancel` (line 653-667): validates job exists, calls `cancel()`, returns `409` if not cancellable, also marks suite cancelled\n- `POST /benchmarks/:id/cancel` (line 544-554): finds the active job for a suite, cancels it, marks suite cancelled\n- Both return `{ jobId, cancelled: true }` on success\n\n### Tests (all passing)\n- **Queued job cancel**: `apps/server/tests/jobs.test.ts:49`, `apps/server/tests/api.test.ts:506`\n- **In-flight job cancel**: `apps/server/tests/jobs.test.ts:68`, `apps/server/tests/api.test.ts:421` and `:599`\n- **Already-finished job cancel**: `apps/server/tests/jobs.test.ts:93`, `apps/server/tests/api.test.ts:699`\n- **BenchmarkService-level cancel**: `packages/benchmark/tests/cancel.test.ts` (8 tests covering queued, in-flight, completed, failed, already-cancelled, non-existent suites, blocked runTask, and stopped runSuite loop)\n\nNo changes are needed — the feature is complete and tested.",
